# Connection.cpp and Cursor.cpp are generated from Connection.xs and
# Cursor.xs by xsubpp, driven by this directory's .xs.cpp rule, and must not
# be tracked (#9678).  the .xs sources and the hand written .pm modules stay
# tracked - this is why the ignore is by name and not *.cpp
/Connection.cpp
/Cursor.cpp

# bootstrap and packlist files the installmod target writes, and the man
# pages installman generates from the .pm files.  3pm is PERLMAN3EXT from
# configure; a perl reporting a different man extension leaves those
# untracked instead
*.bs
*.packlist
*.3pm
